<title>USA: American Management wins 3-yr contract.</title>
<headline>American Management wins 3-yr contract.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFAX, Va. 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Management Systems said on Thursday the Federal Retirement Thrift Investment Board awarded it a three-year, $29 million contract to revamp the retirement plan's record keeping system.</p>
<p>American Management will provide full design services that could offer a daily valuation of accounts, rather than monthly valuations, and give the fund the capability to offer more investment choices.</p>
<p>The Thrift Savings Plan's assets, which are held by 2.3 million current and former federal workers, total about $47 billion.</p>
</text>
